//www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://ds.canonical.com/Layout> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/global.group.tiles> <https://ds.canonical.com/documentationStage> <https://ds.canonical.com/tag.needsdefinition> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/global.group.tiles> <https://ds.canonical.com/tier> <https://ds.canonical.com/global> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/global.group.tiles> <https://ds.canonical.com/guidelines> \"\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/global.group.tiles> <https://ds.canonical.com/usage> \"\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/global.group.tiles> <https://ds.canonical.com/anatomyClassic> \"\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/global.group.tiles> <https://ds.canonical.com/anatomyDsl> \"\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/global.group.tiles> <https://ds.canonical.com/summary> \"\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/global.group.tiles> <https://ds.canonical.com/name> \"Tiles\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/global.group.tiles> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://ds.canonical.com/Group> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/global.group.keyboard_keys> <https://ds.canonical.com/documentationStage> <https://ds.canonical.com/tag.needsdocumentation> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/global.group.keyboard_keys> <https://ds.canonical.com/tier> <https://ds.canonical.com/global> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/global.group.keyboard_keys> <https://ds.canonical.com/guidelines> \"\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/global.group.keyboard_keys> <https://ds.canonical.com/usage> \"KeyboardKeys are used to present multiple keys as a single conceptual unit, like a shortcut or a related key group.\\n\\n\\n\\n**When to use**\\n\\n- To compose modifier and actions keys with a “+” separator between them, e.g. Ctrl + C\\n- Group keys that belong together, such as the four arrow keys, without separators.\\n\\n\\n\\n**When not to use**\\n\\n- When showing only one key, the grouping wrapper adds no value\\n- When grouped items are not keyboard keys\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/global.group.keyboard_keys> <https://ds.canonical.com/anatomyClassic> \"\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/global.group.keyboard_keys> <https://ds.canonical.com/anatomyDsl> \"---\\nnode:\\n  uri: global.group.keyboard_keys\\n  styles:\\n    layout.display: inline-flex\\n    layout.align: center\\n    spacing.gap: spacing/horizontal/xsmall\\n  edges:\\n    - node:\\n        uri: global.component.keyboard_key\\n      relation:\\n        cardinality: \\\"2..*\\\"\\n        slotName: default\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/global.group.keyboard_keys> <https://ds.canonical.com/summary> \"KeyboardKeys groups two or more KeyboardKey components into a single inline unit with consistent spacing. Use it to represent multi-key shortcuts (e.g., Ctrl + C) or key sets (e.g., arrow keys) as a visually cohesive group. It accepts arbitrary children, including separator text, alongside KeyboardKey instances.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/global.group.keyboard_keys> <https://ds.canonical.com/name> \"KeyboardKeys\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/global.group.keyboard_keys> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://ds.canonical.com/Group> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/global.group.code_snippets> <https://ds.canonical.com/documentationStage> <https://ds.canonical.com/tag.needsdefinition> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/global.group.code_snippets> <https://ds.canonical.com/tier> <https://ds.canonical.com/global> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/global.group.code_snippets> <https://ds.canonical.com/guidelines> \"\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/global.group.code_snippets> <https://ds.canonical.com/usage> \"\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/global.group.code_snippets> <https://ds.canonical.com/anatomyClassic> \"\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/global.group.code_snippets> <https://ds.canonical.com/anatomyDsl> \"\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/global.group.code_snippets> <https://ds.canonical.com/summary> \"\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/global.group.code_snippets> <https://ds.canonical.com/name> \"CodeSnippets\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/global.group.code_snippets> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://ds.canonical.com/Group> .\n_:ee452379d2bdf581594ee348278454f9 <https://ds.canonical.com/timestamp> \"2026-04-08T00:00:00.000+02:00\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/global.group.cards> <https://ds.canonical.com/changeLog> _:ee452379d2bdf581594ee348278454f9 .\n_:ee452379d2bdf581594ee348278454f9 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://ds.canonical.com/ChangeLogEntry> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/global.group.cards> <https://ds.canonical.com/documentationStage> <https://ds.canonical.com/tag.needsdefinition> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/global.group.cards> <https://ds.canonical.com/tier> <https://ds.canonical.com/global> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/global.group.cards> <https://ds.canonical.com/guidelines> \"\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/global.group.cards> <https://ds.canonical.com/usage> \"\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/global.group.cards> <https://ds.canonical.com/anatomyClassic> \"\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/global.group.cards> <https://ds.canonical.com/anatomyDsl> \"\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/global.group.cards> <https://ds.canonical.com/summary> \"\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/global.group.cards> <https://ds.canonical.com/name> \"Cards\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/global.group.cards> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://ds.canonical.com/Group> .\n_:e94854ffac1f2583bed07a4f70c71842 <https://ds.canonical.com/optional> \"false\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/global.group.buttons> <https://ds.canonical.com/hasProperty> _:e94854ffac1f2583bed07a4f70c71842 .\n_:e94854ffac1f2583bed07a4f70c71842 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://ds.canonical.com/Property> .\n_:fa72ff754c25e7a044671c6c0af4c981 <https://ds.canonical.com/optional> \"false\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/global.group.buttons> <https://ds.canonical.com/hasProperty> _:fa72ff754c25e7a044671c6c0af4c981 .\n_:fa72ff754c25e7